  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nWith models coming into alignment in bringing a cold front \nthrough late on Wednesday, confidence is increasing in heat relief\non Thursday. North of I-40, we have 30-50% of temperatures below \n90 degrees (virtually all ensemble members keep this area below \n100). Southern Oklahoma and north Texas are likely to be warmer \nwith 40-80% chance of highs below 100 degrees (0-20% chance for \nless than 90). Showers and storms will likely linger into Thursday\nmorning with 20-30% chance for afternoon redevelopment (highest \nchances along the front). Temperatures will depend largely on \nprogression of the front and extent of cloud cover and showers.\n\nWhile models diverge greatly on what the synoptic pattern will \nlook like over the weekend, they do have general agreement that \nthe ridge will continue to exert some influence with positive \n500mb height anomalies over us. Rain chances through this period \nrange from 10-30% (highest in northern Oklahoma). Temperatures \nwill likely be in the 90 to 105 degree range with the warmest \ntemperatures more likely in southern Oklahoma / north Texas. \nBeyond Sunday, the interquartile spread increases to 15 to 25 \ndegrees.\n\nDay",
